WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.570
At a Theravada temple, lay
Buddhists chant five lines in Pali,

2
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.610
after the three refuges.

3
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:12.220
Each one begins the same way: I undertake
the training rule to abstain from.

4
00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.340
Then come killing,
taking what is not given,

5
00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:20.790
sexual misconduct, false speech,
and intoxicating drinks and drugs.

6
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:25.290
No god gives these rules, and no
one enforces them on lay people.

7
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.900
So what happens when one is broken?

8
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:32.350
In this mission, you'll find out why
Buddhists call the precepts training rules,

9
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.050
not commandments.

10
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.610
Then you'll climb a ladder of commitment:

11
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:43.240
5 precepts, then 8, then 10,
then 227 rules for monks.

12
00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:47.960
Your mission: find out what Buddhists
believe follows a broken precept.
